      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Graceville%2C_Queensland",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In December 1911, 207 plots of the Graceville Estate went up for auction, promising a gentle slope toward the river.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Graceville%2C_Queensland",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A Baptist chapel first opened on 22 May 1864 near Oxley Creek, marking the earliest organized worship in the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Graceville%2C_Queensland",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Graceville hosts three notable parks—Simpson’s Playground, Graceville Memorial Park, and Faulkner Park—offering green retreats for locals.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
